From e6f70ef0cc4caea7a56ad602780d227d149ec69e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI Lab <mia.ailab1@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 20:34:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] glm cuda: block FP8 checkpoints (quant_method fp8, e4m3 with
 128 x 128 scales: Z.AI's and unsloth's layout)

A quant_method "fp8" checkpoint with weight_block_size [128, 128] is admitted beside ModelOpt's and EXL3
(cuda_fp8block.zig; another block, a per-tensor FP8 or another code format is refused by name). Its routed experts
load as cuda/experts.zig's fp8g layer (cuda_weights.fp8Experts: gate and up by the rank's rows, down by its inputs,
the codes packed on the host with Fp8Experts.packGateUp and packOne, the fp32 scales cut to the rank's blocks), and
the family's expert kernels carry fp8_experts.cu's decode and prompt forms beside NVFP4's, dispatched by the layer's
format. Every other quantized linear (the dense MLPs, the shared experts, the DSA layers' q_a, q_b, kv_a and o) reads
as the lane's block-FP8 projection (fp8_pb) under a new declared format, fp8_block, that admits bf16 or block FP8 and
nothing else; the dense MLP gains that arm. The scale tensor may be named weight_scale (ModelOpt) or
weight_scale_inv (Z.AI, unsloth): the same multiplier. Routed experts shard at 128 rows, the scale block.
